{-1}=\\,\\,$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ |  |" 13194139534078 true] [17592186277103 1113 #uuid "9dc6b8f7-0245-52df-b551-40892e2a6e3c" 13194139534078 true] [17592186277103 1145 "Given a $2\\times 2$ matrix\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe inverse of $A$ can be found using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the determinant:\n\n$$\ndet(A)=6\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 9=-12\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, then, the inverse is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}[\\begin{aligned}d & -b \\\\ -c & a\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-12}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -9 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1/12 & 1/6 \\\\ 3/4 & -1/2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can verify the result as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A{A}^{-1} & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1/12 & 1/6 \\\\ 3/4 & -1/2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓ \\\\ {A}^{-1}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-1/12 & 1/6 \\\\ 3/4 & -1/2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6 & 2 \\\\ 9 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534078 true] [17592186277104 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277105 13194139534078 true] [17592186277104 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534078 true] [17592186277104 1041 "field-1" 13194139534078 true] [17592186277104 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277105 13194139534078 true] [17592186277104 1110 #uuid "641442f3-70be-5342-a3cc-667686c722f2" 13194139534078 true] [17592186277105 1034 "-\\frac{1}{12}" 13194139534078 true] [17592186277105 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534078 true] [17592186277105 1111 #uuid "2ce6153d-aa59-5359-b219-8c1c198d1afa" 13194139534078 true] [17592186277106 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277107 13194139534078 true] [17592186277106 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534078 true] [17592186277106 1041 "field-2" 13194139534078 true] [17592186277106 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277107 13194139534078 true] [17592186277106 1110 #uuid "6b9e8a32-ea26-5050-869b-a03050ab688f" 13194139534078 true] [17592186277107 1034 "\\frac{1}{6}" 13194139534078 true] [17592186277107 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534078 true] [17592186277107 1111 #uuid "d125b20c-5b8b-5ae6-bd32-8886217f5c5e" 13194139534078 true] [17592186277108 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277109 13194139534078 true] [17592186277108 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534078 true] [17592186277108 1041 "field-3" 13194139534078 true] [17592186277108 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277109 13194139534078 true] [17592186277108 1110 #uuid "4821afe3-ea54-5b82-8dda-386bf8d454c0" 13194139534078 true] [17592186277109 1034 "\\frac{3}{4}" 13194139534078 true] [17592186277109 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534078 true] [17592186277109 1111 #uuid "4d856aa9-aea1-572e-bb1f-46b9b59fd70b" 13194139534078 true] [17592186277110 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277111 13194139534078 true] [17592186277110 1089 "q-316781" 13194139534078 true] [17592186277110 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534078 true] [17592186277110 1100 "If $B=[\\begin{aligned}2x & 5x-1 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}]$\nis a singular matrix, calculate the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534078 true] [17592186277110 1113 #uuid "332a826c-7348-5345-899f-11bdcbd79a2d" 13194139534078 true] [17592186277110 1145 "The matrix $B$ is singular if and only if $det(B)=0.$ Calculating the determinant, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B) & =(2x)\\cdot (-2)-4\\cdot (5x-1) \\\\  & =-4x+4-20x \\\\  & =-24x+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we set the determinant equal to $0$ and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-24x+4 & =0 \\\\ 24x & =4 \\\\ x & =\\frac{4}{24} \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534078 true] [17592186277111 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277112 13194139534078 true] [17592186277111 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534078 true] [17592186277111 1041 "field-1" 13194139534078 true] [17592186277111 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277112 13194139534078 true] [17592186277111 1110 #uuid "90f007b8-4c17-5edb-8319-70889d75f9bc" 13194139534078 true] [17592186277112 1034 "\\frac{1}{6}" 13194139534078 true] [17592186277112 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534078 true] [17592186277112 1111 #uuid "197273cb-fad0-550e-847c-37b81ec3acbd" 13194139534078 true] [17592186277113 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277114 13194139534078 true] [17592186277113 1089 "q-71938" 13194139534078 true] [17592186277113 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534078 true] [17592186277113 1100 "Which of the matrices below does **not** have an inverse?\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 6 \\\\ 10 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,Y=[\\begin{aligned}6 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,Z=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 10 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534078 true] [17592186277113 1113 #uuid "f34f6a84-b6d1-59f1-84c8-b1742c3a5c7a" 13194139534078 true] [17592186277113 1145 "- The matrix $X$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix. So, it is not invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $Y$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(Y)=6\\cdot 6-7\\cdot 5=1.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(Y)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $Y$ is invertible.\n\n- For the matrix $Z$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(Z)=(-2)\\cdot 5-10\\cdot 1=-20.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(Z)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that $Z$ is invertible.\n\nTherefore, only $X$ does not have an inverse." 13194139534078 true] [17592186277114 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277115 13194139534078 true] [17592186277114 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277116 13194139534078 true] [17592186277114 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277117 13194139534078 true] [17592186277114 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277118 13194139534078 true] [17592186277114 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277119 13194139534078 true] [17592186277114 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534078 true] [17592186277114 1041 "selection" 13194139534078 true] [17592186277114 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277119 13194139534078 true] [17592186277114 1110 #uuid 