78 true] [17592186277134 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277135 13194139534078 true] [17592186277134 1089 "q-7915" 13194139534078 true] [17592186277134 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534078 true] [17592186277134 1100 "Which of the matrices below are singular?\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 8 & 6\\end{aligned}],\\,Q=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,R=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139534078 true] [17592186277134 1113 #uuid "17761662-c8e1-5053-be1d-f17ca1632a52" 13194139534078 true] [17592186277134 1145 "- For the matrix $P$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(P)=4\\cdot 6-8\\cdot 3=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(P)=0,$ we conclude that $P$ is not invertible. Since $P$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $P$ is singular.\n\n- For the matrix $Q$, we have\n\n$$\ndet(Q)=1\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot (-1)=0.\n$$\n\nBecause $det(Q)=0,$ we conclude that $Q$ is not invertible. Since $Q$ is a square matrix that is not invertible, we also say that $Q$ is singular.\n\n- The matrix $R$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix. So, it is not invertible. Since the matrix is not square, we can't say that it's singular.\n\nTherefore, only $P$ and $Q$ are singular." 13194139534078 true] [17592186277135 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277136 13194139534078 true] [17592186277135 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277137 13194139534078 true] [17592186277135 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277138 13194139534078 true] [17592186277135 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277139 13194139534078 true] [17592186277135 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277140 13194139534078 true] [17592186277135 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534078 true] [17592186277135 1041 "selection" 13194139534078 true] [17592186277135 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277140 13194139534078 true] [17592186277135 1110 #uuid "074b9c92-0e09-5b09-a3cf-2efb2a6798f7" 13194139534078 true] [17592186277136 1034 "$P$ and $R$ only" 13194139534078 true] [17592186277136 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534078 true] [17592186277136 1111 #uuid "15691103-f36a-518